1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,380
Once again, seething, residual anger has burst forth in an American city.
郁积未消、翻腾不已的怒火，又一次在一座美国城市爆发了。

2
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:14,240
And the riots that overtook Los Angeles were a reminder of what knowledgeable observers have been saying for a quarter-century.
而席卷洛杉矶的这场骚乱，让人想起见多识广的观察人士二十五年来一直在说的话。

3
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:25,830
America will continue paying a high price in civil and ethnic unrest unless the nation commits itself to programs that help the urban poor lead productive and respectable lives.
除非美国致力于推行各项计划，帮助城市贫困人口过上有所作为、体面的生活，否则就将继续付出社会和族群动荡的高昂代价。

4
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:31,360
Once again, a proven program is worth pondering: national service.
有一项行之有效的计划再次值得认真斟酌：国民服役。

5
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:49,240
Somewhat akin to the military training that generations of American males received in the armed forces, a 1990s version would prepare thousands of unemployable and undereducated young adults for quality lives in our increasingly global and technology-driven economy.
20世纪90年代版的国民服役有点类似于一代代美国男性在军队中接受的军事训练，它将让成千上万无法就业、受教育不足的年轻人做好准备，以便在我们这个日益全球化、由技术驱动的经济中过上高质量的生活。

6
00:00:50,040 --> 00:01:03,230
National service opportunities would be available to any who needed it and, make no mistake, the problems are now so structural, so intractable, that any solution will require massive federal intervention.
国民服役的机会将向一切有需要的人开放；而且，毫无疑问，如今这些问题已是如此根深蒂固的结构性问题，又如此棘手，以至于任何解决办法都将需要联邦政府大规模干预。

7
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:19,200
In his much-quoted book, “The Truly Disadvantaged,” sociologist William Julius Wilson wrote that “only a major program of economic reform” will prevent the riot-prone urban underclass from being permanently locked out of American economic life.
社会学家威廉·朱利叶斯·威尔逊在其广为引用的著作《真正的穷人》中写道，“只有一项重大的经济改革计划”才能防止容易发生骚乱的城市底层阶级被永远排斥在美国经济生活之外。

8
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,430
Today, we simply have no choice; the enemy within and among our separate ethnic selves is as daunting as any foreign foe.
如今，我们根本别无选择；敌人就在我们各自隔绝的族群内部和族群之间，和任何外敌一样令人生畏。

9
00:01:28,230 --> 00:01:42,590
Families who are rent apart by welfare dependency, job discrimination and intense feelings of alienation have produced minority teenagers with very little self-discipline and little faith that good grades and the American work ethic will pay off.
因依赖福利、就业歧视和强烈的疏离感而四分五裂的家庭，造就了一批自律能力极差的少数族裔青少年，他们也几乎不相信好成绩和美国式的敬业精神会有回报。

10
00:01:43,390 --> 00:01:49,620
A military-like environment for them with practical domestic objectives could produce startling results.
为他们提供一种类似军队、有着切实国内目标的环境，可能会产生惊人的效果。

11
00:01:50,420 --> 00:02:03,360
Military service has been the most successful career-training program we’ve ever known, and American children born in the years since the all-volunteer Army was instituted make up a large proportion of this targeted group.
兵役一直是我们迄今所知最成功的职业培训计划；而自陆军实行全志愿兵役制以来出生的美国孩子，在这一目标群体中占了很大比例。

12
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:12,390
But this opportunity may disappear forever if too many of our military bases are summarily closed and converted or sold to the private sector.
但如果我们有太多军事基地被草草关闭、改作他用或卖给私营部门，这个机会就可能永远消失。

13
00:02:13,190 --> 00:02:17,850
The facilities, manpower, traditions, and capacity are already in place.
设施、人力、传统和能力都已经到位。

14
00:02:18,650 --> 00:02:21,120
Don’t dismantle it: rechannel it.
不要拆掉它，而要给它改换用途。

15
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:25,890
Discipline is a cornerstone of any responsible citizen’s life.
对任何一个负责任的公民来说，纪律都是其生活的基石。

16
00:02:26,690 --> 00:02:29,750
I was taught it by my father, who was a policeman.
我父亲是一名警察，是他教会了我守纪律。

17
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:33,190
Many of the rioters have never had any at all.
许多参与骚乱的人从来就没有过一丁点纪律。

18
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:38,510
As an athlete and former Army officer, I know that discipline can be learned.
作为一名运动员和前陆军军官，我知道纪律是可以学会的。

19
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:43,100
More importantly, it must be learned or it doesn’t take hold.
更重要的是，纪律必须靠学习得来，否则就扎不下根。

20
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:50,040
A precedent for this approach was the Civilian Conservation Corps that worked so well during the Great Depression.
这种做法有一个先例，那就是大萧条时期成效卓著的民间资源保护队。

21
00:02:50,840 --> 00:03:00,340
My father enlisted in the CCC as a young man with an elementary school education and he learned invaluable skills that served him well throughout his life.
我父亲加入民间资源保护队时，还是个小学文化程度的年轻人；他在那里学到了极其宝贵的技能，这些技能让他终身受益。

22
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:04,340
The key was that a job was waiting for him when he finished.
关键在于，他结业时就有一份工作在等着他。

23
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:13,430
The certainty of that first entry-level position is essential if severely alienated young minority men and women are to keep the faith.
要让严重疏离社会的少数族裔青年男女保持信念，就必须确保他们一定能得到那第一份入门级的工作。

24
00:03:14,230 --> 00:03:22,360
We all know these are difficult times for the public sector, but here’s a chance to add energetic and able manpower to America’s workforce.
我们都知道，如今公共部门正处于困难时期，但眼前就有一个机会，可以为美国的劳动力队伍增添精力充沛、能干的人手。

25
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:30,990
They could be prepared for the world of work or college—an offer similar to that made to returning GIs after World War II.
他们可以为进入职场或上大学做好准备——这和第二次世界大战后向归来的美国大兵提供的机会相似。

26
00:03:31,790 --> 00:03:39,980
It would be a chance for 16- to 21-year-olds to live among other cultures, religions and races and in different geographical areas.
这将让16岁到21岁的年轻人有机会生活在其他文化、宗教和种族的人群之中，生活在不同的地区。

27
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:50,510
And these young people could be taught to rally around common goals and friendships that evolve out of pride in one’s squad, platoon, company, battalion—or commander.
而且还可以教会这些年轻人围绕共同的目标和友谊团结起来，这些目标和友谊源于对自己所在的班、排、连、营，或是对指挥官的自豪感。

28
00:03:51,310 --> 00:03:57,610
We saw such images during the Persian Gulf War and during the NCAA Final Four basketball games.
我们在海湾战争期间和NCAA篮球联赛四强赛期间都看到过这样的画面。

29
00:03:58,410 --> 00:04:09,610
In military life and competitive sports, this camaraderie doesn’t just happen; it is taught and learned in an atmosphere of discipline and earned mutual respect for others’ capabilities.
在军队生活和竞技体育中，这种同袍情谊不会自然而然地产生，而是在纪律严明、彼此凭能力赢得尊重的氛围中教出来、学出来的。

30
00:04:10,410 --> 00:04:26,130
A national service program would also help overcome two damaging perceptions held by America’s disaffected youth: that society just doesn’t care about minority youngsters and that one’s personal best efforts will not be rewarded in our discriminatory job market.
国民服役计划还将有助于消除美国心怀不满的年轻人所持有的两种有害看法：一是社会根本不关心少数族裔青少年，二是在我们这个充满歧视的就业市场中，个人竭尽全力也不会得到回报。

31
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:41,770
Harvard professor Robert Reich’s research has shown that urban social ills are so pervasive that the upper 20 percent of Americans—that “fortunate fifth” as he calls them—have decided quietly to “secede” from the bottom four-fifths in particular.
哈佛大学教授罗伯特·赖克的研究表明，城市社会弊病已普遍到这样的地步：最上层20%的美国人——他称之为“幸运的五分之一”——已经悄悄决定，尤其要“脱离”底层的五分之四。

32
00:04:42,570 --> 00:04:45,790
We cannot accept such estrangement on a permanent basis.
我们不能接受这种隔阂永远存在下去。

33
00:04:46,590 --> 00:04:54,890
And what better way to answer skeptics from any group than by certifying the technical skill of graduates from a national service training program?
而要回应任何群体中的怀疑者，还有什么办法比认证国民服役培训计划结业学员的技术技能更好呢？

34
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:59,650
Now, we must act decisively to forestall future urban unrest.
现在，我们必须果断行动，预防今后的城市动荡。

35
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:06,039
Republicans must put aside their aversion to funding programs aimed at certain cultural groups.
有些计划以特定文化群体为对象，共和党人必须抛开对资助这类计划的反感。

36
00:05:06,839 --> 00:05:19,289
Democrats must forget labels and recognize that a geographically isolated subgroup of Americans—their children in particular—needs systematic and substantive assistance for at least another 20 years.
民主党人必须抛开标签，认识到有一部分美国人在地理上处于孤立状态，他们——尤其是他们的孩子——至少还需要20年系统而实质性的援助。

37
00:05:20,089 --> 00:05:27,039
The ethnic taproots of minority Americans are deeply buried in a soil of faith and loyalty to traditional values.
少数族裔美国人的族群之根，深深埋在信仰和忠于传统价值观的土壤里。

38
00:05:27,839 --> 00:05:41,559
With its emphasis on discipline, teamwork, conflict resolution, personal responsibility and marketable skills development, national service can provide that vital first job that will reconnect these Americans to the rest of us.
国民服役注重纪律、团队合作、化解冲突、个人责任以及培养有市场需求的技能，能提供那至关重要的第一份工作，让这些美国人与我们其余的人重新联系起来。

39
00:05:42,359 --> 00:05:44,669
Let’s do it now before the fire next time.
让我们现在就行动起来，赶在下一场烈火燃起之前。
